old_code/

# Per-experiment plans (sample_info.yaml, measurement_info.yaml, beamtime
# scripts) ARE tracked as of 2026-09-07 -- they are the worked examples a new
# user copies, and expt.user_plan_dir resolves into them from experiment.yml.
# As of 2026-09-08 the throwaway bits are tracked too, by the owner's decision:
# the two rules that used to exclude them are left here, commented, so it is
# clear they were removed on purpose rather than lost.
# src/user_plans/.loglogin
# src/user_plans/**/error_log.txt
#
# NOTE: src/user_plans/.loglogin is STILL ignored despite the line above being
# commented out -- the bare `.loglogin` rule under "APS IT droppings" higher up
# catches it anywhere in the tree. That one is deliberate (it is an APS IT
# dropping, not user content); delete it there too if you really want the file.

# RE metadata dictionary for session persistence
.re_md_dict.yml

# local reference copies
*\ copy.py

# generated run state (id8_common/expt_config.py) -- lives in state/ since
# 2026-09-06. Both patterns are unanchored, so they also catch a stale copy
# left at the repo root by an older checkout. The state/ directory itself does
# not need to exist in a checkout: expt_config.dump() mkdir -p's it.
run_state.yml
.run_state-*
